    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nIn telescope there is a default keybind to edit a command from the command history list <C-e>.\r\n\r\nBelow is an excerpt from the telescope docs:\r\n\r\n```\r\nbuiltin.command_history({opts})          *telescope.builtin.command_history()*\r\n    Lists commands that were executed recently, and reruns them on `<cr>`\r\n    - Default keymaps:\r\n      - `<C-e>`: open the command line with the text of the currently selected\r\n        result populated in it\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs there a way to emulate this behavior when using mini pick's history command?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In telescope there is a default keybind to edit a command from the command history list .</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Below is an excerpt from the telescope docs:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"builtin.command_history({opts})          *telescope.builtin.command_history()*\n    Lists commands that were executed recently, and reruns them on `&lt;cr&gt;`\n    - Default keymaps:\n      - `&lt;C-e&gt;`: open the command line with the text of the currently selected\n        result populated in it\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">builtin.command_history({opts})          *telescope.builtin.command_history()*\n    Lists commands that were executed recently, and reruns them on `&lt;cr&gt;`\n    - Default keymaps:\n      - `&lt;C-e&gt;`: open the command line with the text of the currently selected\n        result populated in it\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to emulate this behavior when using mini pick's history command?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nIn telescope there is a default keybind to edit a command from the command history list .\nBelow is an excerpt from the telescope docs:\nbuiltin.command_history({opts})          *telescope.builtin.command_history()*\n    Lists commands that were executed recently, and reruns them on `<cr>`\n    - Default keymaps:\n      - `<C-e>`: open the command line with the text of the currently selected\n        result populated in it\n\nIs there a way to emulate this behavior when using mini pick's history command?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
